<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-Feb oil output falls 2 pct vs year ago.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-Feb oil output falls 2 pct vs year ago.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia produced 47.2 million tonnes of crude oil in the first two months of 1997, two percent lower than year-ago levels, figures from the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>Committee figures also showed oil product output slipping two percent year-on-year to 28.9 million tonnes over the same period.</p>
</text>
